    \"\u0412\u0435\u0439\u043b\u044c\" \u0432 \u043c\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0438\u043a\u0435
    \u0438\u0437\u0432\u0435\u0441\u0442\u043d\u043e \u043e\u0447\u0435\u043d\u044c \u0445\u043e\u0440\u043e\u0448\u043e,
    \u043d\u043e \u043d\u0435 \u0441\u0442\u043e\u0438\u0442 \u043f\u0443\u0442\u0430\u0442\u044c
    \u043d\u0430\u0448\u0435\u0433\u043e \u0433\u0435\u0440\u043e\u044f \u0441 \u0434\u0440\u0443\u0433\u0438\u043c
    \u0432\u0435\u043b\u0438\u043a\u0438\u043c \u043c\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0438\u043a\u043e\u043c,
    \u0413\u0435\u0440\u043c\u0430\u043d\u043e\u043c \u0412\u0435\u0439\u043b\u0435\u043c. \u041d\u0435\u0441\u043c\u043e\u0442\u0440\u044f
    \u043d\u0430 \u0441\u0445\u043e\u0436\u0443\u044e \u0444\u0430\u043c\u0438\u043b\u0438\u044e
    \u0438 \u043e\u0431\u0449\u0443\u044e \u043e\u0431\u043b\u0430\u0441\u0442\u044c \u043d\u0430\u0443\u043a\u0438,
    \u043e\u043d\u0438 \u043d\u0435 \u0431\u044b\u043b\u0438 \u0440\u043e\u0434\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u0438\u043a\u0430\u043c\u0438.
    \u0410\u043d\u0434\u0440\u0435, \u043e\u0434\u043d\u0430\u043a\u043e, \u0445\u043e\u0440\u043e\u0448\u043e
    \u0437\u043d\u0430\u043b \u0440\u0430\u0431\u043e\u0442\u044b \u0413\u0435\u0440\u043c\u0430\u043d\u0430
    \u0412\u0435\u0439\u043b\u044f \u0438 \u0434\u0430\u0436\u0435 \u043d\u0430\u043f\u0438\u0441\u0430\u043b
    \u043e \u043d\u0438\u0445 \u0441\u0442\u0430\u0442\u044c\u044e."
  interestingFactsEn: "Andre Weil was an outstanding and multifaceted man, so his life is full of unusual facts, some of them.\n\nThe tongues were given to Veil with remarkable ease since his childhood. He began with German, and his parents spoke it when they did not want the children to understand the conversation. Andre and his sister Simona eventually learned the language by eavesdropping on adults. When he was a young man, he was very fond of ancient Greek and Latin, and then of Sanskrit. His passion for Sanskrit was so strong that he determined his way of life (this was the language that led him to India).But that's not all: during his work in Brazil, he taught mathematics in Portuguese, lectured and explained in Russian, and in the United States his main language became English.\n\nAt the beginning of World War II, Weil left France for Finland, and Finland was fighting with the Soviet Union, and the authorities suspected that French mathematician might be a spy.It looked like evidence to the uninformed Finnish police, and in fact, Nickola Burbaki was a collective pseudonym of a group of French mathematicians, one of whose founders was Veil, who, according to legend, saved him from being shot by a famous Finnish mathematician, Rolf Nevanlinna.\n\n♪ Studies and Sanskrit, who set his career Love of Ancient Languages, played a funny role in the fate of Weil, and when he was unable to find a suitable job in France after a brilliant study and dissertation, it was his Sanskrit mentor, Professor Sylvain Levy, who helped him to become head of the Department of Mathematics at the University of Aligarh in India.Thus, his language passion opened the way for him to work in a country he loved in absentia.\n\n♪ No, he's not related to Herman Veil The name \"Vale\" in mathematics is very well known, but we shouldn't confuse our hero with another great mathematician, Herman Weil. Despite the same name and the general field of science, they weren't related. Andre, however, was well aware of Herman Weil's work and even wrote an article about them."
